flow "ZooKeeper leader election"
summary "Servers create ephemeral sequential znodes and watch only their predecessor so leadership transfers cleanly on session expiry without a herd effect."
tags leader-election coordination zookeeper
level advanced
source "https://zookeeper.apache.org/doc/current/recipes.html#sc_leaderElection"
related distributed-systems/leader-lease distributed-systems/raft-consensus

group nodes "Candidate servers"
node s1 "Server 1" service in=nodes tone=primary
node s2 "Server 2" service in=nodes
node s3 "Server 3" service in=nodes
node zk "ZooKeeper Ensemble" db
edge s1 > zk
edge s2 > zk
edge s3 > zk
array znodes "/election znodes" =

scenario elect "Sequential ephemeral znodes pick a leader"
  step create "Each server creates an ephemeral sequential znode"
    "All three servers create an **ephemeral sequential** znode under `/election`. ZooKeeper assigns strictly increasing suffixes: `n_001` (S1), `n_002` (S2), `n_003` (S3)."
    detail "The official ZooKeeper recipe prefixes the path with a client-generated GUID (`/election/<guid>-n_`). If a recoverable connection error drops the `create` response after the server already created the znode, the client can locate its own proposal via `getChildren` instead of creating a duplicate."
    send s1 > zk "create -e -s"
    send s2 > zk "create -e -s" with
    send s3 > zk "create -e -s" with
    values znodes = n_001:S1 n_002:S2 n_003:S3
    state zk active
  step watch "Lowest sequence leads; others watch predecessor"
    "Server 1 owns the smallest znode (`n_001`), so it is leader. Rather than everyone watching `n_001` (which causes a **herd effect**), S2 watches `n_001` and S3 watches `n_002`."
    state s1,znodes#0 success
    state s2,s3 pending
    callout s2 "Watches n_001 only"
    callout s3 "Watches n_002 only" with

scenario session-expiry "Session expiry deletes znode and promotes S2" from=elect/watch
  step expire "Server 1 crashes; session expires"
    "Server 1 loses connectivity and misses ZooKeeper heartbeats. When its session expires, ZooKeeper automatically deletes its **ephemeral** znode `n_001`."
    state s1 error
    effect s1 shake
    values znodes = n_002:S2 n_003:S3
    callout zk "Ephemeral n_001 auto-deleted"
  step notify-s2 "Only Server 2 is notified (no herd effect)"
    "ZooKeeper fires the watch event to **Server 2 only** — Server 3 stays undisturbed because its predecessor `n_002` is still alive."
    send zk > s2 "n_001 deleted!"
    state s2 active
    callout s3 "Not woken up (watches n_002)"
  step promote "Server 2 verifies lowest sequence and leads"
    "Server 2 calls `getChildren(/election)`, confirms `n_002` is now the smallest znode, and safely assumes leadership."
    detail "Re-checking `getChildren` is mandatory: a watch event only proves the immediate predecessor disappeared, which can also happen if a non-leader standby crashes. If a smaller znode still exists, the woken server sets a new `exists` watch on the next-lower predecessor instead of taking leadership."
    send s2 > zk "getChildren"
    send zk > s2 "[n_002, n_003]"
    state s2,znodes#0 success
    callout s2 "New leader: owns smallest znode"
